# Project context

This is a Roblox game built in Roblox Studio, synced to this filesystem via the
Argon extension (Rojo-style project). Code is Luau. Do not assume Node/JS/TS
tooling applies — this is not a web project even though it lives in a synced
folder structure.

Two workstreams live in this workspace (check which one a task belongs to
before writing code):

1. **Sword cultivation game** — my own game project. Core gameplay, sword
   cultivation progression systems, combat.
2. **Environment/VFX gig** — client work. Scope is strictly: lighting,
   atmosphere, terrain, particle effects, general environment polish. Do NOT
   touch gameplay/backend systems for this workstream unless explicitly asked.
   Visual benchmark: Grow a Garden, Catch and Tame, Greedy Growers, Steal an
   Egg — bright, saturated, chunky/stylized, readable-at-a-distance Roblox
   art style. Not realistic/PBR-heavy, not muted/gritty.

# General rules

- Luau conventions: PascalCase for services/instances, camelCase for local
  vars/functions, `local` everything, avoid globals.
- Prefer editing/creating instances via scripts that Argon will sync, not
  by asking me to manually click around Studio — unless the task is genuinely
  easier done by hand (e.g. tweaking a Beam curve visually).
- When writing anything Studio-facing (ParticleEmitter, Beam, Trail, Lighting
  properties, PostEffects), always give me the exact property names/values to
  set, since you cannot see the render output — I'll eyeball it in Studio and
  report back what needs adjusting.
- Don't invent Roblox API members. If unsure an API/property exists, say so
  rather than guessing — Luau/Roblox API hallucinations are expensive to
  debug inside Studio.
- Keep responses focused. Don't refactor unrelated code unless asked.
